   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 812,
   "text": "Most modern color vinyl is on par with black pressings. Other steps in the vinyl record production process, such as mastering and a pressing plant’s quality control standards, have a more substantial impact on playback.\nIt should be noted, though, that clear vinyl, picture discs, and glow-in-the-dark pressings are more susceptible to poor playback. Very few additives can be mixed into clear vinyl ",
