   "tag": "p×2",
   "class": "container max-width-1300 wp-block-paragraph",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 362,
   "text": "If you care most about consistency, black vinyl is the safe bet. For most listeners, the difference isn’t something you’ll notice day to day, though. If you like the look or collectability, color vinyl is a solid choice.\nUltimately, you should buy whichever version of a particular record excited you and inspires you to put on the turntable and drop the needle.",
